# Architecture boundaries

Detailed layer layout lives in `01-architecture.mdc`. This rule is the boundary checklist.

- Before editing, inspect the target feature and a comparable implementation, starting with `lib/features/home/` if it exists.
- Keep widgets, pages, Cubit/Bloc, and UI state in the presentation layer (View + ViewModel).
- Keep entities/models, data sources, and repository contracts/implementations in the data layer.
- Cubit depends on the abstract repository only — do not call Dio, Hive, or data sources from presentation.
- There is no domain or use-case layer; do not introduce one without an explicit request and approval.
- Entities live under `data/models/`. Hive annotations on entities (as in `home` `ProductEntity`) follow that pattern when caching is required.
- Follow the existing `Either<Failure, T>` and `safeCall` pattern where the repository uses it. Do not add a parallel error-handling convention.
- Reuse existing dependency-injection registration conventions and feature injection files. Verify the actual registration flow before changing it.
- Avoid generic abstractions, base classes, or extra layers unless the task requires them and the benefit is explained.
- Do not move or rename public types or folders as part of an unrelated feature.
